      "videos": [],
      "texts": [
        "Pol Muxart",
        "Ballad Studio",
        "Creative Services",
        "[Brand Identity]",
        "Category:",
        "Fashion, Brand Identity, Visual Universe,",
        "Context:",
        "Ballad, a name evoking a magical and mysterious ballad, originated in Barcelona as a handcrafted label defined by bold, expressive cuts. What began as a bespoke project quickly transitioned into styling for celebrities and influencers. Facing the evolution from an artisan atelier to a professional brand, the project required a strategic branding exercise to channel its growth and define its visual identity and universe.",
        "The Challenge:",
        "The primary goal was to transform the codes of traditional tailoring. We sought to redefine formalwear by hybridizing it with an urban, industrial aesthetic and the raw energy of the techno scene. Ballad does not design clothes simply for \"dressing up\"; it creates pieces that navigate avant-garde nightlife without sacrificing sophistication. It is the meeting point between material quality and pattern irreverence.",
        "Concept:",
        "The identity centers on the \u201cUnfitting Uniform\u201d concept, serving as both tagline and narrative axis. It is a manifesto for the misfit\u2014those who refuse to conform. The term is twofold: it addresses social rebellion as much as the physical construction of the garments, which feature dropped crotches and oversize cuts that challenge the conventional fit of traditional tailoring.",
        "Result:",
        "For the logotype, we developed custom lettering that merges a master tailor\u2019s classic signature with abrupt angles and geometric cuts, projecting a sophisticated hardness that rejects the organic. This expressive and formal brand mark contrasts with the industrial rawness of the visual system. The graphic language playing with negatives and typographic displacement to symbolize the concept of \"not fitting in.\"",
        "The art direction relies on high-contrast black and white to elevate the aesthetic, employing negatives, motion blur, and off-center framing to reinforce the \"unfitting\" narrative. Finally, the monogram is constructed by abstracting the brand\u2019s initials into the shape of a butterfly, representing genuine beauty and freedom of movement as a hallmark of quality and identity.",
        "Services:",
        "Creative Direction, Graphic Design",
        "Year:",
        "2026"
      ]
    },
